Diabetes protects against dying in intensive care Possible in principle, but the design gives a simpler explanation that needs no protective effect at all.
ICU admission is a collider, and selecting on it creates a spurious association Correct. Patients without diabetes who reach the ICU tend to have been admitted with more severe acute illness, which carries higher mortality. Restricting the study to ICU patients conditions on the collider.
Diabetes is a confounder that should have been adjusted for Diabetes is the exposure here. The problem is not a missing adjustment but a selection on a variable caused by the exposure and by severity.
