The walk and the sleep tip have hardly been tried, so a better nudge may never be discovered Correct. Greedy choice stops gathering evidence about arms that had an unlucky start. Exploration — random with ε-greedy, or guided by the posterior with Thompson sampling — keeps that possibility open.
The breathing exercise estimate is biased upwards because it was chosen often Choosing an arm often makes its estimate more precise, not biased. The concern is the arms that were not chosen.
Participants will get bored of the same nudge Possibly true in real life, but that is a change in the environment, not the statistical risk of greedy choice that the question is about.



