Without smoothing, almost every letter would get probability zero; with it, every letter gets a probability, but the model will still be poor at predicting them Correct. Cardiology letters contain many word sequences never seen on Ward 7. Smoothing turns “impossible” into “very unlikely”, which keeps the arithmetic working; it does not create knowledge of cardiology.
Smoothing is needed only for bigram models, not trigram models The longer the context, the sparser the counts (Table 16.3), so higher-order models need smoothing more, not less.



