In a diffusion model, which part is learned from data?

The forward process that adds noise The forward process is a fixed recipe, Equation 19.6, chosen by the designer. You ran it in the widget with no training at all.
The noise schedule \(\beta_1, \dots, \beta_T\) In the standard method the schedule is fixed in advance (Ho et al. used a straight line from 0.0001 to 0.02). Some variants tune it, but it is not what makes the model generate.
A network that predicts the noise in a noisy image, used to run the process backwards Correct. All the knowledge of what X-rays look like lives in the denoising network \(\mathbf{\varepsilon}_\theta\), trained with Equation 19.7.
